 this,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'He was led as a sheep to the slaughter;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ(And like a lamb dumb before his shearer,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text»So opened he not his mouth:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ/In his humiliation his judgment was taken away:¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And who shall declare his generation?¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ%For his life is taken from the earth.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And the eunuch answered Philip, and said, I pray thee, of whom speaketh the prophet this? of himself, or of some other man?¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Then Philip opened his mouth, and began at the same scripture, and preached unto him Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book+§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse(¦verses•„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And as they went on their way, they came unto a certain water: and the eunuch said, See, here is water; what doth hinder me to be baptized?¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Philip said, If thou believest with all thine heart, thou mayest. And he answered and said, I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And he commanded the chariot to stand still: and they went down both into the water, both Philip and the eunuch; and he baptized him.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšAnd when they were come up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord caught away Philip, that the eunuch saw him no more: and he went on his way rejoicing.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlBut Philip was found at Azotus: and passing through he preached in all the cities, till he came to CÃ¦sarea.¦layout ªlast_verse(